# My everyday loaf based on morph

grain:
  prairie_gold
  hard_red
  barley = 5%
  spelt = 5%
  buckwheat = 5%

dry:
  grain
  vwg = 3%
  potato_flakes = 5%
  yeast = 0.5%
  salt = 1.8%

wet:
  cold_water
  old_dough = 100g
  flourless_starter = 20%
  ascorbic_acid_1p = 50ppm * 100 * grain
  olive_oil = 5%
  honey = 5%
  sour_cream = 5% # out of yogurt

dough:
  wet
  dry
  old_dough = 0 - wet.old_dough
  hydration = 70%
  # 200g/L of flour
  # total_flour = 660g # 13 inch
  total_flour = 500g # 9 inch
  # total = 1086g

/*
August 7, 2026

Changes
- No leaven, I'm trying old dough and flourless starter only
- double the flas

I started about 7:35

Dry T=92. Wet T=51. 

Used the KA for mixing. Mixed about 8:04. Stopped after 2 minutes;
it cleaned the bowl. DT after mixing is 70F. RT is 76F. 

30 minute rest in fridge.

8:38 Kneaded 10 minutes in KA. It was cleaning the bowl and looking great.

Into the cambro and the fridge at 8:50. S&F every 30 minutes.

Into the pan at 11:00. Left on the counter at 77F.

100g of dough into fridge.

Baked at 12:15 for 45 minutes at 350F lid off.

I added 100ml of water to the pan before preheating the oven.

Beautiful loaf.
Super soft and delicious. Not sour.

*/

